        "payload": {
          "description": "As a TypeScript Engineer, you will work remotely on an hourly paid basis reviewing AI-generated TypeScript code snippets, design proposals, and technical explanations, as well as generating your own high-quality content and reference solutions. You will evaluate step-by-step reasoning and problem-solving, checking solutions for correctness, clarity, and adherence to the prompt; identify errors in logic, type modeling, or architectural thinking; fact-check technical information; craft clear explanations and model solutions that demonstrate correct approaches; and rate and compare multiple AI responses based on their reasoning quality and implementation soundness. This fully remote, hourly contractor position is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI data services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate that provides AI training data to many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation model labs. In this role, your TypeScript expertise directly helps improve the world’s premier AI models used by engineers and developers everywhere.\nImportant\nThere is no immediate project for this role; however, if qualified, you will be among the first experts we reach out to when relevant opportunities arise. This will also provide you with access to future projects available through our expert network.\nKey Responsibilities\nDevelop AI Training Content: Create detailed prompts in various topics and responses to guide AI learning, ensuring the models reflect a comprehensive understanding of diverse subjects.\nOptimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI responses to enhance the model's accuracy, fluency, and contextual relevance.\nEnsure Model Integrity: Test AI models for potential inaccuracies or biases, validating their reliability across use cases.\nYour Profile\n2+ years professional TypeScript experience.\nExpertise in TypeScript features, including advanced type manipulation, generics, interfaces, and utility types.\nStrong proficiency with a major frontend framework (e.g., React, Angular, or Vue.js) or backend runtime (e.g., Node.js with Express or NestJS).\nSolid understanding of object-oriented programming (OOP), functional programming concepts, and common software design patterns.\nExperience with Git and standard version control workflows (branching, merging, pull requests).\nFamiliarity with modern build tools (e.g., Webpack, Vite, Babel).\nMinimum Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or a closely related field.\nMinimum C1 English proficiency (written and spoken), with strong ability to follow detailed technical guidelines.\nGood to have: Merged PRs in TypeScript-based open-source projects.\nGood to have: Competitive programming experience, experience reviewing typed API layers, DTOs, or schema-driven designs, and previous exposure to AI data training or annotation projects.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4475555140": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-31T05:53:06.350550+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "As an hourly paid, fully remote JavaScript Engineer for AI Data Training, you will review complex AI-generated code and explanations or generate new ones, evaluate the reasoning quality and step-by-step problem-solving, and provide expert feedback that helps models produce answers that are accurate, logical, and clearly explained. You will assess solutions for accuracy, clarity, and adherence to the prompt, identify errors in methodology or conceptual understanding, fact-check information, write high-quality explanations and model solutions that demonstrate correct methods, and rate and compare multiple AI responses based on correctness and reasoning quality. This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate that provides AI training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation model labs. Your work will directly help improve the world’s premier AI models while giving you the flexibility of impactful, detail-oriented remote contract work.\nImportant\nThere is no immediate project for this role; however, if qualified, you will be among the first experts we reach out to when relevant opportunities arise. This will also provide you with access to future projects available through our expert network.\nKey Responsibilities\nDevelop AI Training Content: Create detailed prompts in various topics and responses to guide AI learning, ensuring the models reflect a comprehensive understanding of diverse subjects.\nOptimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI responses to enhance the model's accuracy, fluency, and contextual relevance.\nEnsure Model Integrity: Test AI models for potential inaccuracies or biases, validating their reliability across use cases.\nYour Profile\nMinimum 2+ years of professional JavaScript experience in production environments.\nStrong understanding of closures, async/await, prototype-based inheritance, and JavaScript event loop behavior, with deep proficiency in modern Vanilla JavaScript (ES6/ES2015+).\nProven ability to evaluate correctness, readability, and performance of JavaScript code, including identifying subtle logic and edge-case issues.\nHands-on work experience in software engineering, preferably in roles involving code review, mentoring, or technical design discussions.\nSignificant experience using LLMs or AI coding assistants while programming, combined with a critical mindset for validating their output.\nExcellent English writing skills, capable of producing clear, concise, and pedagogical technical explanations.\nStrong proficiency with at least one major frontend framework (such as React, Angular, or Vue.js) or backend runtime (such as Node.js with Express or NestJS).\nMinimum Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or a closely related technical field.\nPrevious experience with AI data training, data annotation, or evaluation of AI-generated technical content is a strong plus; Minimum C1 English proficiency and a highly detail-oriented working style are required.\nPreferred: contributions or merged PRs in JavaScript or TypeScript open-source projects, familiarity with bundlers and tooling (Webpack, Vite, Rollup), frontend–backend integration and Node.js runtime behavior, reviewing typed API layers, DTOs, or schema-driven designs, and experience evaluating frontend logic, async patterns, and state management.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4480561855": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-31T05:53:06.350550+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "At Accenture Federal Services, nothing matters more than helping the US federal government make the nation stronger and safer and life better for people. Our 13,000+ people are united in a shared purpose to pursue the limitless potential of technology and ingenuity for clients across defense, national security, public safety, civilian, and military health organizations.\nJoin Accenture Federal Services, a technology company within global Accenture. Recognized as a Glassdoor Top 100 Best Place to Work, we offer a collaborative and caring community where you feel like you belong and are empowered to grow, learn and thrive through hands-on experience, certifications, industry training and more.\nJoin us to drive positive, lasting change that moves missions and the government forward!\nOur Software Engineers are responsible for developing, maintaining, and enhancing software capabilities that support mission operations and system management across a complex technical environment. We are looking for someone who is enthusiastic about learning, collaborating, and contributing to a high‑performing engineering team.\nWhat you’ll do:\nAssist in the development, testing, and maintenance of software components that support development capabilities and mission‑critical workflows\nDebug and troubleshoot software issues under the guidance of more senior engineers\nImplement enhancements, features, and bug fixes in accordance with established coding standards and configuration‑management practices\nCollaborate with systems engineers and other software developers to understand requirements, document changes, and ensure technical accuracy\nSupport integration and deployment activities across development, test, and operational environments\nParticipate in code reviews and contribute to process improvements and team best practices\nMaintain accurate technical documentation as part of the development lifecycle\nWhat you’ll need:\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related technical field (or equivalent relevant experience)\nFamiliarity with modern programming languages such as Java, Python, C++, or JavaScript\nExposure to cloud technologies, containerization, or DevSecOps concepts\nBonus Points if you have:\nFoundational understanding of software development principles, version control, and debugging practices\nExperience with automated testing frameworks or CI/CD pipelines\nInterest in mission-focused software development, operational systems, or systems engineering\nAbility to work collaboratively in a team environment and communicate effectively\nStrong analytical skills and willingness to learn new tools, technologies, and domain knowledge\nClearance:\nMust have an active Top Secret clearance or higher\nAs required by local law, Accenture Federal Services provides reasonable ranges of compensation for hired roles based on labor costs in the states of California, Colorado, Connecticut, Hawaii, Illinois, Maine, Maryland, Massachusetts, Minnesota, New Jersey, New York, Ohio, Vermont, Virginia, Washington, and the District of Columbia . The base pay range for this position in these locations is shown below. Compensation for roles at Accenture Federal Services varies depending on a wide array of factors, including but not limited to office location, role, skill set, and level of experience. Accenture Federal Services offers a wide variety of benefits. You can find more information on benefits here. We accept applications on an on-going basis and there is no fixed deadline to apply.\nThe pay range for the states of California, Colorado, Connecticut, Hawaii, Illinois, Maine, Maryland, Massachusetts, Minnesota, New Jersey, New York, Ohio, Vermont, Virginia, Washington, and the District of Columbia is:\n$94,000—$187,600 USD\nWhat We Believe\nAs a company wholly dedicated to serving the US federal government, we bring together the best talent to help reinvent how federal agencies operate and deliver greater value for their mission and the American people. We have an unwavering commitment to creating a culture in which all our people are respected, feel a sense of belonging, and have equal opportunity. As a business imperative, every person at Accenture Federal Services has the responsibility to create and sustain a culture where everyone feels welcomed and included. This is grounded in our core values and our experience that hiring and developing great people who reflect different perspectives, experiences, and backgrounds is key to driving innovation and delivering the results that our clients and the country count on.\nEqual Employment Opportunity Statement\nWe believe that no one should be discriminated against because of their differences. All employment decisions shall be made without regard to age, race, creed, color, religion, sex, national origin, ancestry, disability status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital status, citizenship status or any other basis as protected by federal, state, or local law. Our rich diversity makes us more innovative, more competitive, and more creative, which helps us better serve our clients and our communities. For details, view a copy of the Accenture Federal Services Equal Opportunity Policy Statement.\nAccenture Federal Services is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. Additionally, as an Affirmative Action Employer for Veterans and Individuals with Disabilities, Accenture Federal Services is committed to providing veteran employment opportunities to our service men and women.\nRequesting An Accommodation\nAccenture Federal Services is committed to providing equal employment opportunities for persons with disabilities or religious observances, including reasonable accommodation when needed. If you are hired by Accenture Federal Services and require accommodation to perform the essential functions of your role, you will be asked to participate in our reasonable accommodation process. Accommodations made to facilitate the recruiting process are not a guarantee of future or continued accommodations once hired.\nIf you   are being considered for employment opportunities with Accenture Federal Services and need an accommodation for a disability or religious observance during the interview process or for the job you are interviewing for, please speak with your recruiter.\nOther Employment Statements\nApplicants for employment in the US must have work authorization that does not now or in the future require sponsorship of a visa for employment authorization in the United States.\nCandidates who are currently employed by a client of Accenture Federal Services or an affiliated Accenture business may not be eligible for consideration.\nJob candidates will not be obligated to disclose sealed or expunged records of conviction or arrest as part of the hiring process.\nThe Company will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against employees or applicants because they have inquired about, discussed, or disclosed their own pay or the pay of another employee or applicant. Additionally, employees who have access to the compensation information of other employees or applicants as a part of their essential job functions cannot disclose the pay of other employees or applicants to individuals who do not otherwise have access to compensation information, unless the disclosure is (a) in response to a formal complaint or charge, (b) in furtherance of an investigation, proceeding, hearing, or action, including an investigation conducted by the employer, or (c) consistent with the Company's legal duty to furnish information.\nCalifornia requires additional notifications for applicants and employees. If you are a California resident, live in or plan to work from Los Angeles County upon being hired for this position, please click here for additional important information.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4481422146": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-31T05:53:06.350550+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Full Stack AI Developer | Python, React & Automation\nRemote – India or Pakistan | Full-Time\nSalary: $2,000 USD per month (flexible for exceptional talent)\nExperience: 3–5 years preferred | Ability matters more than years\nHelp us build an AI-powered recruitment company.\nAt We Are Revolution , we're building something ambitious: a recruitment business where AI, intelligent automation and great technology power almost everything we do.\nWe operate across the US and European recruitment markets, and we're investing heavily in technology to transform how our business works.\nOur goal is to automate entire workflows — from finding candidates and identifying opportunities to matching jobs, communicating with clients, managing recruitment pipelines and analysing performance.\nWe're looking for a talented Full Stack Developer who loves building things, solving problems and using AI to work faster and smarter.\nYou'll join a small, ambitious engineering team, working closely with our Head of Engineering to turn ideas into working products.\nThis isn't a role where you'll spend your days fixing tickets or making minor changes to somebody else's software.\nYou'll be building real systems, solving real business problems and seeing your work used every day.\nWhat you'll be building\nYou'll work across a variety of exciting projects, including:\nAI Agents: Building intelligent agents using Claude, OpenAI and other AI tools to automate complex business processes.\nFull Stack Applications: Developing internal platforms, dashboards and applications using React, Next.js, Python and FastAPI.\nBusiness Automation: Creating workflows using n8n, Python, APIs and AI to eliminate repetitive manual tasks.\nIntelligent Data Systems: Connecting and organising large volumes of candidate, client and recruitment data.\nSystem Integrations: Connecting Salesforce, recruitment CRMs, email platforms, calling systems and third-party APIs.\nAI-Powered Recruitment Tools: Developing systems that identify opportunities, match candidates to jobs and recommend the next best action.\nInfrastructure & Deployment: Deploying and maintaining reliable, scalable applications using modern cloud platforms.\nYou'll have the opportunity to work on projects from initial idea through to development, deployment and continuous improvement.\nThe skills we're looking for\nEssential:\nStrong experience with Python and JavaScript/TypeScript.\nExperience building full stack applications using React or Next.js.\nExperience developing APIs and backend services, ideally using FastAPI.\nGood understanding of databases, SQL and data structures.\nExperience integrating third-party APIs.\nExperience building automations using n8n, Python or similar tools.\nConfident using AI coding tools such as Claude Code, Cursor or GitHub Copilot.\nAbility to independently solve problems and deliver working software.\nNice to have:\nSupabase or Firebase.\nRender, Railway or similar deployment platforms.\nAI agents, MCP, LLM APIs or agent orchestration.\nSalesforce integrations.\nExperience building data pipelines or large-scale automation systems.\nYou don't need to know every technology listed. We're much more interested in someone who can learn quickly, solve problems and build great software.\nThe type of person who will thrive here\nWe're looking for a genuine builder.\nSomeone who enjoys taking a problem, understanding what needs to happen and figuring out the best way to make it work.\nYou'll probably enjoy this role if you:\nLove coding and building new products.\nAlready use AI tools to make yourself a more productive developer.\nEnjoy learning new technologies and experimenting with new ideas.\nTake ownership rather than waiting for detailed instructions.\nCan work across frontend, backend, databases and automation.\nCare about delivering working solutions, not just writing code.\nCommunicate clearly and enjoy being part of a collaborative team.\nWe value intelligence, curiosity, speed of learning and execution more than impressive CVs or academic qualifications.\nWhy join We Are Revolution?\nBuild with AI every day. You'll work with modern AI tools, automation platforms and emerging technologies on genuine commercial applications.\nWork on meaningful projects. Your software won't sit unused. You'll see the impact of what you build across a growing international business.\nReal responsibility and ownership. You'll be trusted to contribute ideas, make technical decisions and own projects.\nWork alongside experienced leadership. You'll collaborate directly with our Head of Engineering and company leadership, who are committed to investing in technology.\nOpportunity to grow. We're building an increasingly sophisticated technology platform, creating opportunities to develop your skills and responsibilities as the team grows.\nRemote working. Work from India or Pakistan as part of an international team.\nCompetitive compensation. We're looking for capability, not simply the cheapest developer. We'll consider stronger packages for exceptional candidates.\nHow to apply\nWe'd love to hear from you if you're a developer who genuinely enjoys building things and wants to work at the intersection of AI, software engineering and business automation .\nPlease send us your CV, GitHub or portfolio, and tell us briefly:\nWhat's the most interesting application, AI agent or automation you've personally built, and what did it achieve?\nWe care much more about what you've actually built than how many technologies you can list on your CV.\nCome and help us build the future of AI-powered recruitment.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4481451013": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-31T05:53:06.350550+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Introduction\nA career in IBM Consulting is built on long-term client relationships and close collaboration worldwide. You'll work with leading companies across industries, helping them shape their hybrid cloud and AI journeys. With support from our strategic partners, robust IBM technology, and Red Hat, you'll have the tools to drive meaningful change and accelerate client impact. At IBM Consulting, curiosity fuels success. You'll be encouraged to challenge the norm, explore new ideas, and create innovative solutions that deliver real results. Our culture of growth and empathy focuses on your long-term career development while valuing your unique skills and experiences.\nYour Role And Responsibilities\nAs an Application Developer specializing in SAP ABAP HANA, you will design, develop, and support application solutions with a focus on the HANA version of Advanced Business Application Programming (ABAP). You will work on designing, developing, and re-engineering highly complex application components, integrating software packages, programs, and reusable objects residing on multiple platforms.\nYour Primary Responsibilities Will Include\nDevelop Application Solutions: Design, develop, and support application solutions with a focus on HANA version of ABAP, ensuring seamless integration with existing systems and platforms.\nIntegrate Software Packages: Integrate software packages, programs, and reusable objects residing on multiple platforms, leveraging knowledge of SAP HANA Technical Concept and Architecture.\nRe-engineer Application Components: Re-engineer highly complex application components to optimize performance, scalability, and reliability, utilizing ABAP Development Tools (ADT) and Code Performance Rules and Guidelines for SAP HANA.\nModel Data using HANA Studio: Create data models using HANA Studio, adhering to best practices and ensuring data consistency and integrity.\nConsume HANA Live Models: Consume HANA Live models to deliver real-time insights and analytics, leveraging knowledge of ADBC, Native SQL, and ABAP Core Data Services.\nRequired Technical And Professional Expertise\nExposure to SAP ABAP HANA: Experience working with HANA version of Advanced Business Application Programming (ABAP), including designing, developing, and supporting application solutions.\nKnowledge of SAP HANA Technical Concept and Architecture: Familiarity with SAP HANA Technical Concept and Architecture, including data modeling using HANA Studio and ABAP Development Tools (ADT).\nExperience with Data Modeling: Exposure to data modeling using HANA Studio, adhering to best practices and ensuring data consistency and integrity.\nUnderstanding of Code Performance Rules: Familiarity with Code Performance Rules and Guidelines for SAP HANA, including ADBC, Native SQL, and ABAP Core Data Services.\nIntegration Experience: Experience integrating software packages, programs, and reusable objects residing on multiple platforms.\nPreferred Technical And Professional Experience\nWorking Knowledge of HANA Live: Familiarity with consuming HANA Live models to deliver real-time insights and analytics, leveraging knowledge of ADBC, Native SQL, and ABAP Core Data Services.\nExposure to Database Procedures: Understanding of database procedures, text search, and ALV on HANA, including data base procedures and HANA Live models consumption.\nFamiliarity with ABAP Core Data Services: Knowledge of ABAP Core Data Services, including data modeling and code performance optimization techniques.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
