          "description": "Be part of a team that unleashes the power of leading-edge technologies to help improve the health and well-being of those most vulnerable in our country and communities. Working at Gainwell carries its rewards. You’ll have an incredible opportunity to grow your career in a company that values work flexibility, learning, and career development. You’ll add to your technical credentials and certifications while enjoying a generous, flexible vacation policy and educational assistance. We also have comprehensive leadership and technical development academies to help build your skills and capabilities.\nSummary\nYour role in our mission\nEssential Job Functions\nCodes, tests, debugs, implements, and documents basic programs. Assists in the modification of company products and/or customer/internal systems to meet the needs of the client and/or end-user.\nAssists in the research and analysis of existing systems and program requirements; assists in preparing documentation to change existing programs. Performs data analysis to support internal and external project needs.\nDesigns basic programs for projects or enhancements to existing programs.\nWrites specifications for programs of low to moderate complexity.\nAssists in resolving routine production support problems.\nAssists in the completion of unit testing by preparing test data, running tests and evaluating results. Develops screen tests and debugging problems. Develops test plans to verify logic of new or modified programs.\nCreates basic documentation in work assignments such as program code.\nConducts routine quality assurance activities such as peer reviews.\nRemains abreast of and researches industry technical trends and new development to maintain current skills and remain current with industry standards.\nBasic Qualifications\nWhat we're looking for\nZero or more years of experience in programming or testing\nExperience working in a student employment program or related experience\nExperience working with appropriate programming languages, operating systems and software\nExperience working with relational databases to facilitate programming software\nOther Qualifications\nBasic programming skills\nPersonal computer and business solutions software skills\nAnalytical and problem solving skills for design, creation and testing of programs\nInterpersonal skills to interact with team members\nCommunication skills to work effectively with team members, support personnel, and clients\nWhat You Should Expect In This Role\nFully remote opportunity with the option to work anywhere within the United States\nOpportunities to travel through your work (0-10%)\nWillingness to work a flexible schedule to accommodate business needs and travel as required\nVideo cameras must be used during all interviews, as well as during the initial week of orientation\nThis posting is intended for pipelining. We will accept applications on an ongoing basis.\nThe pay range for this position is 46,600 -66,600 per year, however, the base pay offered may vary depending on geographic region, internal equity, job-related knowledge, skills, and experience among other factors. Put your passion to work at Gainwell. You’ll have the opportunity to grow your career in a company that values work flexibility, learning, and career development. All salaried, full-time candidates are eligible for our generous, flexible vacation policy, a 401(k) employer match, comprehensive health benefits, and educational assistance. We also have a variety of leadership and technical development academies to help build your skills and capabilities.\nWe believe nothing is impossible when you bring together people who care deeply about making healthcare work better for everyone. Build your career with Gainwell, an industry leader. You’ll be joining a company where collaboration, innovation, and inclusion fuel our growth. Learn more about Gainwell at our company website and visit our Careers site for all available job role openings.\nGainwell Technologies is an Equal Opportunity Employer, where all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, gender (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical condition), age, sexual orientation, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, or other applicable legally protected characteristics. Gainwell Technologies defines “wages” and “wage rates” to include “all forms of pay, including, but not limited to, salary, overtime pay, bonuses, stock, stock options, profit sharing and bonus plans, life insurance, vacation and holiday pay, cleaning or gasoline allowances, hotel accommodations, reimbursement for travel expenses, and benefits.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4482592882": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-31T05:53:06.350550+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Position Description & Qualifications\nWe are seeking a Junior Software Engineer to support a DoD program. The candidate will work with the technical lead and development team to maintain and enhance existing Java-based applications in the cloud environment, troubleshoot issues, and support ongoing development and modernization efforts. The position offers opportunities to learn Python, APEX and other application development tools, as well as gain hands-on experience to AI-assisted development practices already being used by the team. Prior experience with AI technologies is not required, we are looking for someone with a solid Java foundation, strong problem-solving skills, and a willingness to learn new technologies. The candidate will be a self-starter, team-player and will be expected to manage and complete their tasks in a fast-paced results driven environment.\nThis position is fully remote, and candidates may be located anywhere within the United States. Candidates must have an interim or active Secret security clearance.\nIn This Role, You Will\nContribute to all phases of the development lifecycle.\nWrite well designed, testable, and efficient code.\nCode, design, and implement Java and APEX solutions for the Army.\nConduct software analysis, programming, testing, debugging activities and maintenance.\nDevelop technical designs for application development and recommend changes to improve established application processes.\nTo Be Successful In This Role, You Must Have\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science.\nAn interim or active Secret security clearance.\n1 year of relevant IT experience.\nExperience with software development lifecycle.\nExperience with Java software design, development, testing, and deployment.\nExperience with web-based applications, client/server applications, or cloud-hosted systems.\nAbility to travel 10%.\nAdditional Desired Qualifications\nExperience with software development concepts and Agile methodologies.\nExperience with common release tracking software (JIRA, Confluence).\nExperience with basic SQL.\nKnowledge of AWS Cloud.\nKnowledge of leveraging AI-assisted development tools, automated code generation, or AI-powered engineering capabilities.\nIf you are interested in working with a dedicated Serco team, then submit your application now for immediate consideration. It only takes a few minutes!\nCompany Overview\nSerco Inc. (Serco) is the Americas division of Serco Group, plc. In North America, Serco’s 9,000+ employees strive to make an impact every day across 100+ sites in the areas of Defense, Citizen Services, and Transportation. We help our clients deliver vital services more efficiently while increasing the satisfaction of their end customers. Serco serves every branch of the U.S. military, numerous U.S. Federal civilian agencies, the Intelligence Community, the Canadian government, state, provincial and local governments, and commercial clients. While your place may look a little different depending on your role, we know you will find yours here. Wherever you work and whatever you do, we invite you to discover your place in our world. Serco is a place you can count on and where you can make an impact because every contribution matters.\nTo review Serco benefits please visit: https://careers.serco-na.com/us/en/what-we-offer. If you require an accommodation with the application process please email: careers@serco-na.com or call the HR Service Desk at 800-628-6458, option 1. Please note, due to EEOC/OFCCP compliance, Serco is unable to accept resumes by email.\nCandidates may be asked to present proof of identity during the selection process. If requested, this will require presentation of a government-issued I.D. (with photo) with name and address that match the information entered on the application. Serco will not take possession of or retain/store the information provided as proof of identity. For more information on how Serco uses your information, please see our Applicant Privacy Policy and Notice.\nSerco does not accept unsolicited resumes through or from search firms or staffing agencies without being a contracted approved vendor. All unsolicited resumes will be considered the property of Serco and will not be obligated to pay a placement or contract fee. If you are interested in becoming an approved vendor at Serco, please email Agencies@serco-na.com.\nSerco is an equal opportunity employer. We evaluate qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, and other legally protected characteristics.\nPay Transparency\nOur Total Rewards package includes competitive pay, performance-based incentives, and benefits that promote well-being and work-life balance—so you can thrive both professionally and personally. Eligible employees also gain access to a wide range of benefits from comprehensive health coverage and health savings accounts to retirement plans, life and disability insurance, and time-off programs that support work-life balance. Program availability may vary based on factors such as contract type, location, hire date, and applicable collective bargaining agreements.\nSalary range: The range for this position can be found at the top of this posting. This range is provided as a general guideline and represents a good faith estimate across all experience levels. Actual base salary will be determined by a variety of factors, including but not limited to, the scope of the role, relevant experience, job-related knowledge, education and training, key skills, and geographic market considerations. For roles available in multiple states, the range may vary to reflect differences in local labor markets. In addition to base salary, eligible positions may include other forms of compensation such as annual bonuses or long-term incentive opportunities. Benefits – Comprehensible benefits for full-time employees (part-time employees receive a limited package tailored to their role):\nMedical, dental, and vision insurance\nRobust vacation and sick leave benefits, and flexible work arrangements where permitted by role or contract\n401(k) plan that includes employer matching funds\nTuition reimbursement program\nLife insurance and disability coverage\nOptional coverages that can be purchased, including pet insurance, home and auto insurance, additional life and accident insurance, critical illness insurance, group legal, ID theft protection\nBirth, adoption, parental leave benefits\nEmployee Assistance Plan\nTo review all Serco benefits please visit: https://careers.serco-na.com/us/en/about-us.\nSerco complies with all applicable state and local leave laws, including providing time off under the Colorado Healthy Families and Workplaces Act for eligible Colorado residents, in alignment with our policies and benefit plans. The application window for this position is for no more than 60 days. We encourage candidates to apply promptly after the posting date, as the position may close earlier if filled or if the application volume exceeds expectations. Please submit applications exclusively through Serco’s external (or internal) career site. If an applicant has any concerns with job posting compliance, please send an email to: careers@serco-na.com.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4483001473": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-31T05:53:06.350550+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "This is a Fully Remote Job\nAbout Our Client:\nQuora operates in the knowledge sharing and artificial intelligence space, addressing the challenge of organizing and distributing collective intelligence on a global scale. The organization provides two main platforms: a knowledge sharing site with millions of monthly users, and a cloud workspace for running AI agents collaboratively. This setup supports a wide user base and integrates multiple AI models, highlighting the company's emphasis on leveraging machine learning to enhance information access and collaboration.\nAbout the Opportunity:\nThe SOFTWARE ENGINEER NEW GRAD, MACHINE LEARNING PLATFORM role focuses on developing and maintaining the infrastructure that supports large-scale machine learning models. This position contributes directly to the reliability, efficiency, and scalability of ML systems that serve hundreds of millions of users, enabling machine learning engineers to work more effectively. The role offers hands-on experience with distributed systems, GPU serving, and ML platform modernization, impacting the long-term success of the organization's core products.\nResponsibilities:\nBuild and maintain core infrastructure for the machine learning platform ensuring availability and scalability\nDevelop distributed systems for serving diverse machine learning models in production\nOptimize GPU model serving to improve latency, throughput, and cost efficiency\nContribute to platform standardization and modernization efforts\nCreate tools to enhance machine learning engineer productivity\nModernize feature store for faster feature deployment\nParticipate in on-call rotations to manage production issues\nRequirements:\nAvailability during coordination hours (Monday to Friday, 9am to 3pm Pacific Time)\nExpected 2025 or 2026 graduate in Computer Science, Engineering, or related technical field\nInterest in large-scale distributed systems and machine learning infrastructure\nFamiliarity or ability to learn Python, Go, or C++\nCommitment to continuous learning and team improvement\nPay Range and Compensation Package:\nFor US-based applicants, the salary is $97,600\nBenefits & Perks:\nMedical insurance\nVision insurance\nDental insurance\nEqual Opportunity Statement: Our client is an equal opportunity employer. They celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or national origin.\nNote:\nTalentHop is a recruitment partner of this role. Please note that all employment decisions, including candidate assessment, interviews, hiring, compensation, and employment terms, are made exclusively by the hiring employer.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4483012427": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-31T05:53:06.350550+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "This is a Fully Remote Job\nAbout Our Client:\nThis organization operates in the software engineering sector, focusing on developing internal tools, services, workflows, and AI-powered products that support engineering, operations, and recruiting platforms. It addresses the challenge of creating scalable, reliable software systems that enhance internal processes and productivity. The company is positioned to impact the engineering and operational efficiency through innovative platform capabilities.\nAbout the Opportunity:\nThe SOFTWARE ENGINEER, NEW GRAD role is designed for recent graduates and early-career engineers aiming to accelerate their professional growth by building production software systems. This position involves contributing to and eventually owning core internal platform capabilities and product features. The role is critical in supporting internal workflows and platforms, ensuring the delivery of reliable, maintainable, and scalable software solutions.\nResponsibilities:\nContribute to the design and development of end-to-end fullstack systems supporting critical internal workflows and platforms.\nBuild maintainable backend services and APIs following scalable engineering practices.\nDevelop high-quality frontend interfaces for internal teams and end users.\nParticipate in data modeling and database optimization, including schema design and query performance.\nCollaborate with product, operations, and design teams to translate concepts into production-ready features.\nImprove engineering quality through code reviews, testing, documentation, and continuous improvements.\nAssist in troubleshooting production issues to build resilient and observable systems.\nDevelop engineering judgment to balance speed, scalability, and maintainability.\nRequirements:\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Software Engineering, or related field (recent graduate or soon to graduate).\nExperience through internships, co-ops, research, or personal projects in software application development.\nStrong fundamentals in JavaScript and/or TypeScript.\nFamiliarity with frontend development using React or similar frameworks.\nFamiliarity with backend development using Node.js (NestJS is a plus).\nUnderstanding of relational databases such as PostgreSQL and data modeling principles.\nKnowledge of RESTful APIs and distributed application communication.\nExposure to Git and modern software development workflows.\nStrong problem-solving skills, curiosity, attention to detail, and a growth mindset.\nMotivation to learn quickly and contribute in a fast-paced engineering environment.\nPreferred:\nInternship or professional software engineering experience.\nExposure to cloud platforms like AWS, GCP, or Azure.\nFamiliarity with CI/CD, deployment pipelines, or DevOps fundamentals.\nExposure to modern architectures such as microservices, serverless, or event-driven systems.\nInterest in AI-powered products, workflow automation, or data-intensive applications.\nExperience contributing to team projects, hackathons, open-source software, or startup environments.\nPay Range and Compensation Package:\nThe pay range and compensation package for this role will be determined based on the candidate's experience, skills, and other relevant factors.\nEqual Opportunity Statement: Our client is an equal opportunity employer. They celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or national origin.\nNote:\nTalentHop is a recruitment partner of this role. Please note that all employment decisions, including candidate assessment, interviews, hiring, compensation, and employment terms, are made exclusively by the hiring employer.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4483024193": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-31T05:53:06.350550+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "This is a Fully Remote Job\nAbout Our Client:\nThe organization operates in the financial technology sector, focusing on accounts payable automation. It addresses challenges related to reducing costs, preventing overpayments, detecting fraud, and ensuring policy compliance throughout the invoice-to-payment process. By leveraging AI technology, the company supports finance teams in managing these complex workflows effectively.\nAbout the Opportunity:\nThe SOFTWARE ENGINEER role is designed for an early-to-mid-career professional seeking significant ownership and growth within a small engineering team. This position involves developing and maintaining backend features, addressing production issues, and enhancing system reliability for a mature financial platform. The engineer will play a key role in delivering secure, accurate, and efficient solutions that directly impact customer experience and operational integrity.\nResponsibilities:\nDevelop, test, and maintain backend product features primarily using Python, Django, and relational databases.\nUtilize AI-assisted coding tools for problem investigation, implementation, testing, and documentation improvement.\nCritically evaluate AI-generated code for correctness, security, and performance.\nTranslate customer feedback into actionable technical problems and solutions.\nManage tasks from investigation through deployment and follow-up.\nBuild and maintain APIs, asynchronous jobs, integrations, internal tools, and data workflows.\nWrite clear, maintainable code with automated test coverage.\nParticipate in code reviews and technical discussions.\nEnhance system reliability, observability, documentation, and development processes.\nEnsure financial correctness, data integrity, and customer privacy.\nTake increasing ownership of features and technical decisions.\nRequirements:\nEarly-to-mid-career professional software engineering experience.\nStrong Python programming skills.\nExperience with relational databases including design, querying, and debugging.\nFamiliarity with APIs, automated testing, Git, and collaborative development.\nExperience using AI-assisted coding tools responsibly.\nStrong debugging skills and attention to data impact.\nUnderstanding of application concerns like authorization, concurrency, retries, and failure handling.\nClear written and verbal communication.\nCareful approach to handling sensitive financial data.\nComfortable with broad ownership in a small team environment.\nCuriosity, humility, and willingness to learn.\nPay Range and Compensation Package:\nSalary Range: USD 130,000 to 155,000 per year plus annual bonus.\nBenefits & Perks:\nMedical, Dental, and Vision insurance for employees and their families.\nEmployer-sponsored 401(k) plan with company match.\nEqual Opportunity Statement: Our client is an equal opportunity employer. They celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or national origin.\nNote:\nTalentHop is a recruitment partner of this role. Please note that all employment decisions, including candidate assessment, interviews, hiring, compensation, and employment terms, are made exclusively by the hiring employer.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4483025130": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-31T05:53:06.350550+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "This is a Fully Remote Job\nAbout Our Client:\nThis team operates within the Workflow pillar, focusing on communication technologies including calling, messaging, voicemail, transcription, and their supporting workflows. The organization develops interfaces utilized by thousands of businesses daily, aiming to enhance communication tools through scalable and reliable solutions.\nAbout the Opportunity:\nThe FRONTEND ENGINEER will contribute to building and improving critical communication interfaces. This role involves re-architecting calling systems, developing dashboards and tools for performance observability, and shipping new features that enhance user experience. The engineer will own projects end to end, collaborate with cross-functional teams, and support ongoing improvements in calling, messaging, voicemail, and transcription.\nResponsibilities:\nRe-architect calling infrastructure and standardize integration with calling providers\nDevelop dashboards and tools to monitor calling performance\nImplement new features such as URL unfurling, custom transcript summaries, group messaging, direct messages, and calling enhancements\nManage projects from initiation to delivery with senior engineer support\nImprove existing features, fix bugs, and update documentation\nWrite tests and ensure safe deployment through delivery pipelines\nRequirements:\nExperience with React and TypeScript\nUnderstanding of data flow from backend to frontend, including GraphQL and schema design\nAbility to write integration and unit tests, preferably using Playwright\nProblem-solving skills and collaborative approach to building user experiences\nKnowledge of web performance, observability, and accessibility concepts\nStrong ownership and communication skills\nTeam player mindset with willingness to contribute through bug fixes and documentation\nProactive and self-driven in a remote work environment\nMethodical approach to testing and quality assurance\nEmpathy and thoughtfulness in evaluating tradeoffs\nCuriosity and a drive for continuous learning\nClean, readable, testable, and maintainable code practices\nOpenness to integrating AI tools into engineering work\nNice to have:\nExperience with real-time messaging technologies such as WebSockets and WebRTC\nFamiliarity with CI/CD pipelines and mature delivery processes\nExperience with agentic AI workflows for feature generation and testing\nPay Range and Compensation Package:\nSF Bay Area, Los Angeles, Seattle, Portland, Boston, New York, and Washington, DC Metro: $170,000 - $200,000 USD annually\nAll other US Locations: $153,000 - $180,000 USD annually\nCanada: $156,000 - $183,000 CAD annually\nCompensation includes equity, extensive medical coverage, a monthly lifestyle stipend, and a flexible PTO policy\nEqual Opportunity Statement: Our client is an equal opportunity employer. They celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or national origin.\nNote:\nTalentHop is a recruitment partner of this role. Please note that all employment decisions, including candidate assessment, interviews, hiring, compensation, and employment terms, are made exclusively by the hiring employer.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4483045601": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-31T05:53:06.350550+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About Vertex Infinity\nVertex Infinity is a growing tech startup that builds web and mobile applications for clients ranging from startups to large enterprises. We work with AI and large language models to build scalable products from scratch. We’re a small, close-knit team where everyone learns fast, takes ownership and grows with the company.\nAbout the Role\nWe’re looking for a skilled Full Stack Developer to build and maintain complete web applications, from user interface to server and database. You’ll work closely with our designers and founders on real client projects, including AI-powered products.\nWhat You’ll Do\nDevelop full-stack web applications using React.js / Next.js and Node.js\nBuild and maintain REST APIs and back-end services\nDesign and manage databases (MongoDB, PostgreSQL or MySQL)\nConvert Figma designs into responsive, pixel-perfect interfaces\nIntegrate third-party services and AI APIs (OpenAI, Claude, etc.)\nWrite clean, scalable and maintainable code\nDebug, test and optimize applications for performance\nCollaborate with the team on planning and delivering new features\nFull details of the role will be discussed during the interview.\nWhat We’re Looking For\n1–3 years of experience in full-stack development\nStrong knowledge of JavaScript (ES6+); TypeScript is a plus\nHands-on experience with React.js / Next.js on the front end\nHands-on experience with Node.js / Express.js on the back end\nExperience with MongoDB, PostgreSQL or MySQL\nExperience with REST APIs, Git and version control\nFamiliarity with cloud deployment (AWS, Vercel or similar) is a plus\nExperience with AI/LLM integrations is a strong plus\nA portfolio or GitHub profile showing your work\nTiming: 1:00 PM – 10:00 PM, Monday – Friday\nLocation: Thokar Niaz Baig, Lahore (on-site only)",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4483422876": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-31T05:53:06.350550+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "AI Automation & Full-Stack Product Engineer\nWhat if AI could do more than just write a caption?\nCould it help launch and optimise ads?\nBuild landing pages?\nTurn an idea into copy, static creatives and scripts?\nGenerate UGC-style content?\nAutomate reporting?\nAnswer internal questions?\nHandle repetitive client communication?\nHelp our team make better decisions faster?\nThat’s what we want to find out and build.\nCerealBox is looking for its first in-house AI Automation & Full-Stack Product Engineer : someone who can take a real business problem, figure out the smartest technical solution, build it, launch it, maintain it and continuously improve it as better AI models and tools become available.\nThis isn’t a role where someone gives you a list of tickets every morning.\nYou’ll be expected to ask:\n“Why are we doing this manually?”\n“Can AI solve this?”\n“Should we build it ourselves or integrate an existing tool?”\n“How do we make this 10x better?”\nAnd then actually make it happen. 🚀\nA little about CerealBox\nWe’re a UK-based creative and performance agency working exclusively with charities.\nWe manage digital fundraising and paid media for around 30 charity clients and have already built our own analytics platform, True ROAS , to connect advertising spend with actual donation revenue.\nNow we want to take the next step.\nWe want AI and automation embedded across the business not because it sounds cool, but because it can genuinely help our team work smarter, move faster and deliver better results for charities.\nYour first big responsibility\nYou’ll take ownership of True ROAS , our existing production platform used by our media buyers, creative team and leadership.\nToday, it already handles:\nAttribution between Meta Ads and donation data\nROAS reporting by client, campaign and creative\nThousands of creatives and performance insights\nCommercial and settlement reporting\nScheduled data syncs and API integrations\nCurrency conversion and system monitoring\nYou’ll maintain it, improve it and help decide what it becomes next.\nThen comes the fun part 🤖\nSome of the problems we want you to explore include:\nAI Copywriting: Can AI consistently produce strong advertising copy?\nCreative Generation: Can static ad concepts and designs be automated?\nScript Writing: Can AI develop better hooks, concepts and video scripts?\nUGC: How much of UGC production can be generated using AI?\nVideo Editing: Can AI take raw footage and produce high-quality finished ads?\nMedia Buying: Can an AI agent help launch, monitor and optimise campaigns?\nCreative Ideation: Can AI generate genuinely interesting campaign concepts rather than generic ideas?\nLanding Pages: Can we rapidly generate and optimise fundraising landing pages?\nReporting: Can reporting become almost completely automated?\nInternal AI Assistant: Can we make tools like Toast smarter so our team can simply ask questions and get useful answers?\nClient Communication: Can AI safely respond to common or repetitive queries?\nWorkflow Automation: Can we remove repetitive operational work across the company?\nMeta + LLM Integrations: How can Meta data interact with models such as Claude and other LLMs?\nYou won't necessarily build every idea exactly as described.\nPart of your job is deciding what is actually worth building.\nWhat you’ll do\n🧠 AI & Automation\nIdentify repetitive work that can be automated\nResearch AI tools, APIs, models and agents\nPrototype solutions quickly\nDecide whether we should build, integrate or buy\nTurn successful experiments into reliable production tools\nKeep our AI systems current as models and technologies evolve\n💻 Full-Stack Engineering\nBuild and maintain modern React and TypeScript applications\nOwn backend architecture, APIs and database logic\nWork extensively with PostgreSQL and Supabase\nBuild reliable third-party integrations\nMaintain scheduled jobs and data pipelines\nMonitor failures and make sure systems are reliable and secure\n🎨 Product & UX\nSpeak directly with the people using your tools\nUnderstand the actual problem before writing code\nDesign simple, useful interfaces\nTake features from rough idea → prototype → production\nMeasure whether people actually use what you build\nImprove products based on real feedback\nOur current stack\nFrontend\nReact • Vite • TypeScript • TanStack Router & Query • Tailwind • shadcn/ui\nBackend & Data\nSupabase • PostgreSQL • Edge Functions • pg_cron • Row-Level Security\nHosting\nVercel\nIntegrations\nMeta Marketing API • Fundraising platform APIs • AI/LLM APIs\nWays of working\nGitHub • Pull Requests • AI-assisted development\nAnd yes if you can show us that part of the stack should change, we’re open to the conversation.\nWe’d love to speak to you if you have\n4+ years of professional software engineering experience\nStrong full-stack experience with React and TypeScript\nSolid PostgreSQL, data modelling and API experience\nExperience owning production systems\nExperience integrating third-party APIs\nStrong product thinking — not just coding from specifications\nThe ability to design clean interfaces without waiting for perfect Figma files\nConfidence working independently and making technical decisions\nCuriosity around AI, automation, agents and LLM APIs\nClear communication with non-technical teammates\nEven better if you’ve worked with\nSupabase\nMeta Marketing API\nPerformance marketing or ad-tech\nMarketing analytics\nClaude, OpenAI or other LLM APIs\nAI agents / tool calling / MCP\nData visualisation\nCharity or fundraising technology\nEarly-stage products or agencies\nYou do not need to tick every single box.\nIf you’ve built real products, love figuring things out and can show us interesting things you’ve shipped, we’d still like to hear from you.\nWhat you’ll get\n✨ A genuinely high-ownership role\n🤖 The freedom to experiment with AI and emerging technology\n🚀 The opportunity to build products that are actually used every day\n🌍 Exposure to an international UK-based agency environment\n💡 Direct access to leadership and the people using what you build\n📚 Space to research, test and introduce better technology\n🏖️ 21 days paid annual leave\n❤️ Work that ultimately helps charities raise more money\nWhat success looks like\nWe don’t simply want a longer codebase.\nWe want:\nless repetitive work, better data, smarter tools, faster decisions and AI systems that genuinely make the CerealBox team better at what it does.\nIf reading this already has you thinking, “I know how I’d build that…” we should probably talk. 👀\n📩 Apply with your CV, LinkedIn/GitHub profile and, most importantly, examples of products, automations or AI-powered tools you’ve actually built.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4483527878": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-31T05:53:06.350550+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Job Objective\nYour role as Software Engineer is to independently design, develop, test, and maintain full-stack software solutions across backend and frontend layers. You will own assigned features from requirement analysis through implementation, integration, QA handover, and production support, while ensuring solutions are reliable, maintainable, secure, and aligned with established engineering standards.\nMain Tasks\nDesign, develop, and maintain backend services, APIs, business logic, data processing, frontend applications, dashboards, portals, forms, reporting screens, internal tools, and reusable components.\nOwn assigned features from requirement analysis through development, testing support, QA handover, defect resolution, and production support, with limited supervision.\nImplement complete end-to-end features covering frontend user interactions, backend processing, PostgreSQL data persistence, event queue processing, integrations, and final user or system responses.\nDesign and consume REST APIs, including request and response models, validations, authentication, authorization, error handling, and appropriate integration behavior.\nImplement and maintain integration flows with internal services, operators, aggregators, third-party systems, callbacks, and webhooks, ensuring proper error handling and operational visibility.\nDevelop and validate PostgreSQL queries and database interactions, including transaction behavior, indexing, constraints, data persistence, and consistency requirements for assigned features.\nImplement and support RabbitMQ and event-driven workflows, including event publishing, message consumption, payload validation, retries, dead-letter handling awareness, logging, and queue-processing monitoring.\nImplement and support asynchronous workflows such as notifications, billing triggers, delivery reports, background jobs, audit events, and integration callbacks according to system requirements.\nAnalyze business and technical requirements, identify implementation gaps and dependencies, and propose appropriate technical approaches for assigned features before development.\nTroubleshoot and resolve technical issues across backend services, APIs, frontend behavior, PostgreSQL results, event queues, integrations, asynchronous processes, and end-to-end application flows.\nPerform unit testing, support integration and regression testing, resolve identified defects, and validate implemented changes before QA handover and release.\nOptimize standard application performance, including API response times, frontend rendering behavior, PostgreSQL queries, database interactions, and event-processing efficiency.\nCollaborate with QA, Product, DevOps, Support, Security, and other engineering teams to resolve dependencies and ensure smooth end-to-end delivery.\nProvide basic technical guidance to Junior Software Engineers when required and support them in resolving straightforward development and troubleshooting issues.\nEscalate complex architectural, scalability, security, performance, event-driven design, and production-critical concerns to Senior or Lead Software Engineers when required.\nMaintain technical documentation covering APIs, integrations, frontend components, database interactions, event flows, application workflows, configurations, and known technical limitations.\nEnsure development activities comply with Jira traceability, Git and branching practices, pull request and code review requirements, SonarQube validation, secure coding, documentation, and release standards.\nQualifications\nBachelor’s degree in computer science, Software Engineering, Computer Engineering, Information Technology, or a related field.\n2+ years of experience in software development across backend and frontend applications.\nHands-on experience developing and integrating APIs, databases, and full-stack application features.\nExperience with database-driven applications, event-driven or asynchronous processing, and system integrations.\nExposure to messaging, real-time, high-volume, or integration-heavy platforms is considered an advantage.\nProfessional proficiency in Local Language and English is required.\nGood hands-on knowledge of backend development using Java or C#.NET and frontend development using React and Next.js.\nGood understanding of REST APIs, authentication, authorization, integration patterns, callbacks, webhooks, and error handling.\nGood knowledge of PostgreSQL, SQL queries, transactions, indexing fundamentals, constraints, data persistence, and validation.\nGood understanding of RabbitMQ or similar event-queuing technologies, including producers, consumers, message handling, retries, dead-letter concepts, and asynchronous processing.\nAbility to independently develop and troubleshoot complete features across backend, frontend, database, integration, and event-processing layers.\nGood knowledge of Git workflows, branching strategies, pull requests, code reviews, and development traceability.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4483574501": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-31T05:53:06.350550+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Work Week: Sunday - Thursday\nWork Timings: Sunday to Thursday, 9:00 AM – 6:00 PM (KSA time)\nAbout Us\nAt Soum, we're on a mission to build a marketplace that enables users to buy and sell anything online with convenience, trust, and ease, starting in the MENA market. We began with second-hand electronics in KSA, becoming market leaders, and are now expanding to used cars and collectibles. In just two years, we've facilitated hundreds of thousands of transactions across 150+ locations in the Kingdom, maintained 10,000 active listings at any given time, earned the distinction of being the 10th most downloaded e-commerce app in KSA for 2023, and received more than 5 million app downloads.\nJob Summary\nWe are seeking a skilled and motivated Backend Software Engineer to join our dynamic team. As a Backend Software Engineer, you will play a critical role in designing, developing, and maintaining scalable backend systems and microservices that power our products.\nIf you have a strong foundation in backend development, enjoy solving complex problems, and thrive in a collaborative environment, we want to hear from you.\nRole & Responsibilities\nDesign, develop, and maintain backend systems using Node.js, TypeScript, and Nest.js.\nBuild and manage scalable microservices architecture with a focus on performance and reliability.\nDevelop APIs and handle inter-service communication using gRPC.\nWork with MongoDB, PostgreSQL, and ClickHouse for data modeling, storage, and optimization.\nCollaborate with cross-functional teams to understand requirements and deliver high-quality solutions.\nEnsure code quality and maintainability through best practices, code reviews, and testing.\nTroubleshoot, debug, and optimize backend systems to ensure seamless performance.\nRequirements & Qualifications\nRequired Skills\nDesign, develop, and maintain backend systems using Node.js, TypeScript, and Nest.js.\nBuild and manage scalable microservices architecture with a focus on performance and reliability.\nDevelop APIs and handle inter-service communication using gRPC.\nWork with MongoDB, PostgreSQL, and ClickHouse for data modeling, storage, and optimization.\nStrong understanding of CI/CD pipelines and deployment strategies.\nFamiliarity with cloud platforms like AWS, GCP, or Azure.\nKnowledge of distributed systems and event-driven architectures.\nQualifications\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.\n4–5+ years of hands-on experience in backend software development.\nProficient in Node.js and TypeScript.\nExperience working with MongoDB and PostgreSQL in production environments.\nSolid understanding of microservices architecture and communication protocols like gRPC.\nStrong problem-solving skills and attention to detail.\nExcellent communication and collaboration skills.\nNice to Have\nHands-on experience with Kubernetes and Docker.\nExposure to Golang for building performant backend components.\nExperience in scaling and optimizing backend systems for high-traffic applications.\nWe may use artificial intelligence (AI) tools to support parts of the hiring process, such as reviewing applications, analyzing resumes, or assessing responses and identifying potential inconsistencies or verification signals in application materials based on available information. These tools assist our recruitment team but do not replace human judgment. Final hiring decisions are ultimately made by humans. If you would like more information about how your data is processed, please contact us.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4484026797": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-31T05:53:06.350550+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Overview\nGovCIO is hiring a Frontend Developer to build and modernize federal applications on a serverless AWS GovCloud stack. The developer starts with a focus on frontend work and is expected to grow into a full-stack role.\nThis position is remote within the Continental United States (CONUS).\nJob Description\nA GovCIO Frontend Developer works inside a cross-functional product team with designers, backend developers, DevOps engineers, and test engineers. The developer builds and maintains modern web applications using JavaScript, React, and Redux, integrating them with REST APIs on a serverless AWS backend. Strong skills in JavaScript patterns and practices, frontend frameworks, and CSS/SASS are essential. The role is hands-on and deadline-driven. Work starts and finishes inside the sprint. The developer works from user stories and designer wireframes, builds accessible and secure user interfaces, and understands how the frontend and serverless backend fit together. This Frontend Developer position is expected to grow into a full-stack developer role, building backend services with Python and AWS serverless technologies such as API Gateway, Lambda, and Step Functions. Skills in AWS, Python, and AI coding assistants is essential for this growth.\nResponsibilities\nBuild and maintain React and Redux applications in JavaScript.\nIntegrate frontends with REST APIs on AWS API Gateway and Lambda.\nBuild backend services in Python on AWS serverless technologies as you grow into full-stack work.\nIntegrate AI features built on large language models and vision models into applications, including prompt and context engineering.\nBuild applications that handle non-deterministic AI output, where the same input can produce different valid results.\nBuild pages from designer wireframes using CSS and SASS.\nMeet Section 508 and WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility standards.\nApply frontend security practices, including OWASP guidelines, authentication, JWT handling, and PHI/PII protection.\nMaintain the frontend build chain and keep dependencies current.\nWrite unit and component tests. Build and maintain Cypress end-to-end tests in the CI/CD pipeline.\nSubmit and review GitHub pull requests.\nTake part in sprint planning, backlog refinement, and estimation. Write user stories and tasks in Jira.\nPost daily status updates in Jira.\nSupport UAT, Authority to Operate (ATO), and security compliance activities.\nQualifications\nRequired Skills and Experience\nEducation: Bachelor's degree (required) in computer science, information systems, engineering, mathematics, or a related STEM field, with 5 to 10 years of professional frontend or full-stack development experience. A bachelor's degree in a non-STEM field is acceptable when combined with equivalent professional software engineering experience, technical certifications, or completed technical coursework (such as an accredited bootcamp or graduate certificate).\n5+ years of JavaScript development.\n2+ years of React, including Redux or similar state management.\n2+ years of CSS and SASS.\nExperience integrating frontends with REST APIs on a serverless backend (AWS API Gateway, Lambda).\nPython for backend development.\nFamiliarity with machine learning and AI, especially large language models and vision models.\nAutomated testing experience, including Cypress and Jest or similar.\nGit and GitHub pull request reviews.\nAgile/Scrum experience.\nStrong written and verbal communication skills.\nWilling to earn an AWS Associate certification within the first 9 months.\nClearance : Public Trust.\nPreferred Skills And Experience\nAWS Associate Certification: Architect, Developer, or CloudOps\nML basics: training versus inference, overfitting, and class imbalance.\nGenerative AI fundamentals: tokenization, context windows, hallucination, and temperature.\nNET Core and C# for legacy application maintenance.\nFrontend security: OAuth/OIDC, JWT, Amazon Cognito.\nAWS services such as S3, CloudFront, and CloudWatch.\nBuild tools such as npm, Webpack, or Vite.\nAI coding assistants, especially Claude Code.\nHuman-centered design.\nVA or federal program experience.\nPosted Salary Range: USD $90,000.00 - USD $110,000.00 /Yr.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4484040948": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-31T05:53:06.350550+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Job Purpose\nWe are looking for a highly skilled Java Developer with strong experience in Spring Boot and Microservices architecture. The ideal candidate will design, develop, and maintain scalable backend services in a cloud-native environment.\nKey Result Areas\n• Design and develop RESTful APIs using Java 8/11/17\n• Build microservices using Spring Boot\n• Implement service-to-service communication (REST, Kafka, etc.)\n• Work with relational and NoSQL databases\n• Write clean, testable, production-grade code\n• Participate in architecture discussions and technical design\n• Implement security using JWT/OAuth2\n• Optimize application performance and scalability\n• Follow CI/CD and DevOps practices\n• Troubleshoot production issues and perform root cause analysis\nKnowledge, Skills and Experience\n• Strong experience in Java & OOP concepts\n• Hands-on experience with Spring Boot\n• Experience building Microservices architecture\n• Experience with REST APIs\n• Database experience (SQL, PostgreSQL, Oracle, MongoDB)\n• Understanding of Docker & Kubernetes\nExperience with Git\n• Familiarity with CI/CD pipelines",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4484280001": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-31T05:53:06.350550+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Overview\nWorking at Atlassian\nAtlassians can choose where they work – whether in an office, from home, or a combination of the two. That way, Atlassians have more control over supporting their family, personal goals, and other priorities. We can hire people in any country where we have a legal entity.\nTo help our teams work together effectively, this role is fully remote, but requires you to be located in either US Pacific or Mountain time zones .\nYour future team\nWe're hiring a Front End Software Engineer, reporting to an Engineering Manager. Here, you'll work closely with design and product management, influencing the direction of the product and collaborating with team to get there. You'll write code and ship product capabilities that you are proud of and delivering amazing results that our customers love and help us become the best project management tool for business teams!\nResponsibilities\nResponsibilities\nDeliver projects autonomously, from technical design to launch\nBuild client code that is efficient, fast, testable, scalable, and high quality.\nPromote collaboration with other engineers, designers and managers to understand user pain points and iterate to deliver solutions\nPartner with design and product and across other engineering teams to develop delightful customer experiences\nContribute to code reviews and documentation, and take on complex bug fixes\nCompensation\nAt Atlassian, we strive to design equitable, explainable, and competitive compensation programs. We follow consistent hiring practices and account for each candidate's skills, knowledge, and experience when setting base pay within the range.\nPlease visit go.atlassian.com/payzones for more information on which locations are included in each of our geographic pay zones. However, please confirm the zone for your specific location with your recruiter.\nThis role may also be eligible for benefits, bonuses, commissions, and equity.\nPay Ranges\nRole\nIn The United States , we have three geographic pay zones. For this role, our current base pay ranges for new hires in each zone are:\nZone A : $150,300 - $196,225\nZone B : $135,270 - $176,603\nZone C : $124,749 - $162,867\nQualifications\nQualifications\n2+ years of experience building large-scale frontend applications using React.\nBachelor's degree with a preference for Computer Science degree\nUnderstanding of modern frontend ecosystem, including but not limited to bundling, linting, testing and releasing.\nExperience with modern testing frameworks (e.g., Jest, Cypress, Mocha, Chai)\nFamiliarity of the JavaScript language and ecosystem\nExperience building frontend applications at scale\nExperience in Agile software development methodologies\nExperience engineering software systems of medium-to-large scope and complexity\nBenefits & Perks\nAtlassian offers a wide range of perks and benefits designed to support you, your family and to help you engage with your local community. Our offerings include health and wellbeing resources, paid volunteer days, and so much more. To learn more, visit go.atlassian.com/perksandbenefits .\nAbout Atlassian\nAt Atlassian, we're motivated by a common goal: to unleash the potential of every team. Our software products help teams all over the planet and our solutions are designed for all types of work. Team collaboration through our tools makes what may be impossible alone, possible together.\nWe believe that the unique contributions of all Atlassians create our success. To ensure that our products and culture continue to incorporate everyone's perspectives and experience, we never discriminate based on race, religion, national origin, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, or marital, veteran, or disability status. All your information will be kept confidential according to EEO guidelines.\nTo provide you the best experience, we can support with accommodations or adjustments at any stage of the recruitment process. Simply inform our Recruitment team during your conversation with them.\nTo learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit go.atlassian.com/crh .\nIn line with local law, identity verification (which may include use of biometric data) is a condition of employment with Atlassian for employment fraud purposes.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4484442793": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-31T05:53:06.350550+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About Contour\nContour Software has grown from a dozen people to over 2,000 staff across 3 cities, in less than 14 years.\nAs a subsidiary of Constellation Software Inc., we are proud to be part of a global enterprise software conglomerate that has grown to become one of the top 10 software companies in the world, with employees and customers in 100+ countries. With a broad-based and ever-growing portfolio of market-leading, vertical-market enterprise solutions covering more than 100 industry domains in predominantly mature markets, CSI's recipe creates the perfect environment for professionals to build fulfilling, long-term careers.\nWhat started as an R&D & Accounting back-office, has progressed into a full-service Global Centre serving all functions and departments, at the divisional as well as operating group/corporate level. Today Contour employees, located in Karachi, Lahore & Islamabad, are serving CSI divisions located in time zones spanning the globe, from Sydney to Vancouver. With the global growth of Constellation as the wind in our sails, we are only just getting started!\nThe Division\nJonas Premier Construction - a division of Constellation Software Inc. – is the market-leading cloud-based integrated construction management solution, for mid-sized General Contractors, Design Builders and Land Developers. Constellation companies are leading developers of technology solutions for vertical markets in North America, Europe and Australia. Jonas Software is the valued technology partner of over 8000 customers worldwide in 15 countries. Jonas is headquartered in Canada and also operates offices in the United States, the United Kingdom, and the Caribbean.\nThe Position\nWe are looking for Trainee Software Developers to join one of our R&D teams. The selected candidates will be trained for 3 to 3.5 months to become good developers capable of working on enterprise-level applications. After the end of the internship period, there is a good possibility of full-time employment based on satisfactory performance during the internship.\nThe chosen individuals will work out of the Contour Software Lahore resource center office, as an extension of the division-based R&D department.\nRequired Qualifications & Skills\nBS/MS in Computer Science or related field.\nStrong understanding of object-oriented programming principles.\nGood programming concepts and knowledge of .NET programming\nExposure to Generative AI, LLMs, RAG, Prompt Engineering, or AI-powered application development.\nStrong competencies in data structures, algorithms, and software design.\nStrong relational database concepts with SQL queries.\nGood level of knowledge of REST APIs.\nExperience and knowledge of Git.\nA quick learner, with attention to detail, and a commitment to meet deadlines.\nKnowledge of professional software engineering practices\nGood programming concepts and knowledge of frontend programming with JavaScript, AngularJS/Angular.\nGood communication skills in English.\nDisclaimer: At Contour, we attribute our success to the unique contributions of our diverse staff. We’re committed to fostering a culture of respect that thrives on the varied perspectives and experiences of all individuals we recruit, employ, promote, and compensate. Since day one, we’ve adhered to a policy that champions a work environment honoring the worth and dignity of each person while being free from all forms of employment discrimination.\nIn our continuous effort to promote inclusivity, we extend our commitment to individuals with special needs by providing reasonable accommodations. We actively encourage qualified individuals with special needs to apply for the various openings within our company. Should you require assistance in completing the application process or have any inquiries regarding special facilities, please do not hesitate to contact our HR team. Your unique talents and abilities are welcomed and valued here.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4484468525": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-31T05:53:06.350550+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Job Title: Full Stack Engineer, Product Experience\nLocation: Remote (United States)\nTeam: Engineering\nPartner: The fast-growing sports gaming platform in the U.S., backed by top-tier investors.\nAbout\nOur hiring partner is on a mission to build the best products and the biggest company in the fastest-growing consumer industry in America. They believe sports are for everyone and are creating a new tomorrow for every fan. Founded just a few years ago, this innovative company has already built some of the most widely played fantasy games in the market and uniquely launched its own sportsbook on proprietary, homegrown technology—a first in the industry. This allows them to craft distinct, engaging, and seamless experiences that competitors cannot match.\nTheir thesis is simple but powerful: build the best products and the fans will follow. They unite fantasy sports, sports betting, and prediction markets within one intuitive app, constantly pushing the boundaries of what a sports technology company can be.\nWhy This is a Unique Opportunity\nImpact at Scale: Build features used by millions of passionate sports fans. Your work will directly shape the daily experience of a massive, engaged user base.\nOwn Cutting-Edge Products: Contribute to a unified platform that spans multiple high-growth verticals (fantasy, sportsbook, predictions), all built on unique, proprietary technology.\nHigh-Agency Culture: Your voice matters. You will have real influence in technical discussions and product direction from day one.\nRemote-First Excellence: Join a connected, virtual-first culture with a highly engaged distributed workforce, representing one of the most dynamic remote startup jobs in tech today.\nAbout the Role\nWe are looking for a Frontend Engineer to work on cutting-edge projects that gamify and enhance the user experience across our flagship products. This is a unique opportunity to design and build clean, reusable, and performant front-end features that will be used by millions of sports fans.\nYou will collaborate closely with product managers, designers, and backend engineers to deliver elegant and responsive web experiences. This role contributes directly to the upkeep and evolution of our design system, ensuring consistency and quality at a rapid pace.\nWhat You'll Do\nDesign, build, and maintain user-facing features and web experiences for a high-traffic, multi-product platform.\nCollaborate in a cross-functional team to translate product vision into robust, maintainable, and delightful user interfaces.\nContribute to and help evolve our shared component library and design system to ensure consistency and accelerate development.\nWrite high-quality, well-tested code and participate in peer reviews to uphold engineering best practices.\nActively participate in technical and product discussions, bringing your unique perspective to help solve complex challenges.\nWho You Are\nA product-minded engineer with 3+ years of professional experience building modern, consumer-facing web applications.\nYou possess a solid understanding of React and its modern ecosystem (Hooks, Context API, functional components).\nYou have a strong grasp of JavaScript (ES6+), TypeScript, and experience with state management solutions.\nYou are comfortable integrating with and designing around RESTful APIs.\nYou excel at cross-functional collaboration with designers, product managers, and other engineers.\nYou have a strong attention to detail and a commitment to creating high-quality, user-centric experiences.\nYou are familiar with testing frameworks (e.g., Jest, React Testing Library) and modern build tooling (Webpack, Vite).\nYou are an excellent communicator with a collaborative, product-forward mindset.\nEven Better If You Have\nExperience with tools like Amplitude, DataDog, or Storybook.\nA passion for sports or gaming products.\nTech Stack\nReact, TypeScript, JavaScript (ES6+), Material UI, HTML5, CSS3, AWS, Kubernetes, Kafka, Python, ExpressJS\nWhat We Can Offer You\nUnlimited PTO: We're extremely flexible with the exception of a few key weeks around major seasons.\nFamily Support: 16 weeks of fully paid parental leave.\nRemote Work Support: A home office stipend to set up your ideal workspace.\nConnected Culture: A virtual-first culture with a highly engaged, distributed workforce.\nComprehensive Benefits: 5% 401k match, FSA, and company-paid health, dental, and vision plan options for you and your dependents.\nApply Now\nIf you are a talented frontend engineer who cares deeply about your craft, thrives in a high-agency environment, and wants to build products for millions of fans, we encourage you to apply. This is a premier opportunity among remote startup jobs for those looking to join a rocketship in the exciting intersection of sports, gaming, and technology.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4484521392": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-31T05:53:06.350550+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "We are looking for a Full Stack Engineer to join our dynamic team.\nWe build scalable web applications using React/NodeJS/PostgreSQL. Our core technologies are Next.js and Supabase.\nThe ideal candidate has a strong foundation of backend logic & databases and has production experience.\nYou will be working directly with clients abroad on exciting cutting edge products.\nWho we are\nAZKY Tech Labs is a UK/Dubai based agency that specializes in building AI powered solutions (SaaS, Internal tools etc) for clients around the world. Over the past 5 years, we have worked with more than 100 foreign companies (startups, SMEs and Enterprises) in USA, UK, EU and Australia.\nWho You Are\nYou're a good fit if you have strong foundations and production experience in React/Node/PostgreSQL.\nAvailability : This role is for immediate hiring. It is not suitable for candidates who are currently employed full-time in another role.\nPrimary Interest : You have a strong, demonstrable passion for backend development. Your primary interest must be in server-side logic, APIs, and databases, not just UI development.\nTechnical Foundation : You must have solid experience with React.js, Node.js (ideally building REST APIs, e.g., with Express), Relational Databases (e.g., PostgreSQL or MySQL). You have architected databases from scratch.\nCore Concepts : You have a strong grasp of Data Structures, Algorithms, and Client-Server Architecture.\nKey Responsibilities\nDesign, develop, and maintain web and mobile applications\nWrite clean, maintainable, and efficient code following industry best practices.\nCollaborate with QA, and product teams to deliver robust features.\nOptimize application performance, scalability, and security.\nTroubleshoot, debug, and resolve technical issues across the stack.\nParticipate in code reviews, provide feedback, and ensure code quality.\nStay updated with emerging technologies and frameworks to enhance development efficiency.\nSoft skills\nGood English\nStrong attention to detail\nProactive, independent working style\nStrong communication and teamwork skills\nEffective time management and ability to prioritize tasks\nDesire to learn and grow as a developer\nSalary Range: Competitive\nPerks for you\nQuarterly Performance Bonus- based on performance and client outcomes\nCompany equipment (up to PKR 130k allowance to upgrade workstation)\nLaptop allowance (when you use your own laptop)\nInternet backup\nMedical insurance (dependents and parents included)\nDirect communication with clients and PMs (US, UK, EU) on a regular basis\nPaid time off\nFully remote and open work culture",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4484599302": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-31T05:53:06.350550+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Job Summary\nWe are looking for a motivated and enthusiastic Junior Software Engineer to join our development team in Karachi. The ideal candidate should have a strong foundation in programming, a willingness to learn new technologies, and the ability to work collaboratively with senior developers to build and maintain high-quality software applications.\nKey Responsibilities\nAssist in designing, developing, testing, and maintaining software applications.\nWrite clean, readable, and maintainable code under the guidance of senior developers.\nIdentify, troubleshoot, and fix basic software bugs and technical issues.\nAssist in developing and integrating APIs and database solutions.\nParticipate in code reviews and follow software development best practices.\nCollaborate with team members to understand project requirements.\nWrite and maintain technical documentation.\nLearn and implement new tools, frameworks, and technologies.\nParticipate in team meetings and Agile/Scrum development activities.\nRequirements\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.\nBasic knowledge of at least one programming language, such as JavaScript, Python, Java, C#, or PHP.\nUnderstanding of object-oriented programming and fundamental data structures.\nBasic knowledge of databases such as MySQL, PostgreSQL, or MongoDB.\nFamiliarity with Git and version control systems.\nBasic understanding of APIs, software testing, and debugging.\nStrong problem-solving and analytical skills.\nGood communication skills and a willingness to learn.\nPreferred Qualifications\nInternship experience or personal software development projects.\nFamiliarity with frameworks such as React, Node.js, Django, .NET, or Spring Boot.\nBasic understanding of web development and responsive design.\nKnowledge of Agile development methodologies.\nWhat We Offer\nCompetitive salary based on skills and experience.\nMentorship and technical guidance from experienced developers.\nOpportunities for learning and professional growth.\nA collaborative and supportive work environment.\nExposure to real-world software development projects.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4484925065": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-31T05:53:06.350550+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "This employer is hiring a skilled Front-End Specialist to design and build accessible, high-performing user interfaces for complex web applications. The role focuses on delivering seamless digital experiences while ensuring strict adherence to accessibility standards and modern development practices.\nThe Role\n• Design, develop, and maintain responsive, accessible user interfaces using modern JavaScript frameworks.\n• Integrate front-end applications with back-end services and CMS-driven platforms.\n• Build and maintain reusable component libraries to enforce consistent design and coding standards.\n• Ensure all deliverables comply with rigorous accessibility requirements through automated and manual testing.\n• Collaborate with cross-functional teams to translate requirements into user-friendly, secure solutions.\nWhat You'll Need\n• Bachelor’s degree in a technical field or 4 years of equivalent professional experience.\n• 8+ years of experience in front-end or UI development.\n• Expert proficiency in HTML5, CSS3, and modern JavaScript (ES6+), with strong experience in React or Angular.\n• Ability to obtain and maintain a Public Trust clearance, which requires U.S. Citizenship.\nWhat's On Offer\n• Annual salary of $100,001 – $140,000.\n• Opportunity to work in a remote environment on large-scale, impactful projects.\n• Professional development through mentorship and the use of industry-leading best practices.\nApply via Haystack today!",
