      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4485235005": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-31T05:53:06.350550+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Summary\nDo you want to contribute to the development of reliable business applications and AI powered solutions while progressively building the skills needed to take ownership of features, integrations, and AI agent implementations?\nKUKA's Business Apps team develops and maintains software solutions supporting Backoffice operations across the AMER region. We are looking for a motivated Junior Software Developer to join our team and contribute to the development of modern business applications, AI powered solutions, and intelligent automation.\nThis position is ideal for a recent graduate or someone passionate about software development who is eager to learn, experiment with new technologies, and grow alongside an experienced team. Professional experience is not required. We value curiosity, problem solving skills, initiative, and a strong willingness to learn.\nNOTE: Although this is a remote role, we will only consider those who are within commutable distance of our corporate office in Sterling Heights, MI as there will be some occasional onsite requirements.\nKey Responsibilities\nDevelop and maintain web applications, APIs, and integrations supporting business processes.\nContribute to AI agent development using the Microsoft Agent Framework (MFA).\nHelp integrate AI capabilities into existing applications and enterprise systems.\nWork with cloud technologies, primarily Microsoft Azure, to build and deploy software solutions.\nCollaborate with experienced developers on software design, testing, code reviews, and continuous improvement.\nExplore new technologies and identify opportunities to use AI and automation to improve business processes.\nRequired Qualifications\nKnowledge of programming fundamentals and object-oriented programming.\nExperience with at least one programming language through academic projects, personal projects, internships, or professional work.\nInterest in web development, APIs, and modern software architectures.\nStrong problem-solving skills and a willingness to learn new technologies.\nGenuine interest in artificial intelligence, particularly AI agents and software development automation.\nGood communication skills and ability to work collaboratively in a team.\nPreferred Qualifications\nFamiliarity with JavaScript, TypeScript, React.js, C#, or ASP.NET Core.\nBasic understanding of REST APIs, SQL databases, and version control tools such as Git.\nExposure to Microsoft Azure or another cloud platform.\nPersonal, academic, or professional projects involving AI, automation, or web applications.\nFamiliarity with AI development tools or agent frameworks is a plus but not required.\nKUKA is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to building an inclusive and diverse workforce. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, age, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other factor protected by applicable federal, state or local laws.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4485241646": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-31T05:53:06.350550+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Uniti is a premier insurgent fiber provider dedicated to enabling mission-critical connectivity across the United States.\nWith a steadfast commitment to customer service, operational excellence, and superior network capabilities, Uniti builds, operates and delivers critical fiber-based communications services to connect and empower people and businesses.\n_________________________________________________________\nAbout The Role\nThe Software Developer II is responsible for designing, developing, supporting, and improving software solutions that help automate operational workflows and improve service delivery. This role works closely with engineering, operations, and business stakeholders to build reliable backend services, APIs, and automation tools in a collaborative remote environment. The ideal candidate brings strong Python and SQL skills, sound software engineering practices, and the ability to manage work effectively across Azure DevOps, GitHub repositories, and Microsoft Teams.\nWhat You'll Do\nDesign, build, test, deploy, and support software applications, APIs, and automation tools that improve team efficiency and service quality.\nDevelop backend services and integrations using Python and SQL in support of operational and business processes.\nCreate and maintain REST APIs and service integrations with internal systems, databases, and third-party/vendor platforms.\nWrite clean, maintainable, and secure code with attention to performance, reliability, logging, and error handling.\nAnalyze business and technical requirements, translate them into technical solutions, and support successful implementation.\nManage work items, user stories, and sprint-related activities in Azure DevOps (ADO), including story updates, task tracking, and status communication.\nUse Git and GitHub repositories for source control, branching, code review, pull requests, and release coordination.\nCollaborate with cross-functional teams through Microsoft Teams chats, channels, meetings, and other remote communication tools.\nEngage with stakeholders to gather requirements, provide updates, clarify priorities, and support solution adoption.\nSupport troubleshooting, root cause analysis, and issue resolution for production and non-production environments.\nParticipate in an on-call or after-hours support rotation as needed to support critical systems, deployments, or issue resolution.\nWork effectively in a remote environment while managing priorities, meeting deadlines, and maintaining strong communication with the team.\nDo You Have\nCollege degree and 3-5 years of related software development experience, or 7+ years of equivalent engineering/technical experience, or a combination of education and related experience.\nProfessional software development experience with a strong emphasis on backend development.\nStrong Python development experience in production or enterprise environments.\nStrong SQL skills, including writing complex queries, troubleshooting data issues, and working with relational databases.\nExperience developing or supporting REST APIs and system integrations.\nExperience with Git-based source control and collaborative development practices, including pull requests and code reviews.\nExperience working in Agile environments with Azure DevOps or similar work management tools.\nStrong analytical, problem-solving, and troubleshooting skills.\nStrong written and verbal communication skills and the ability to work effectively with technical and non-technical stakeholders.\nTechnical Skills - Python and Backend Development\nStrong proficiency in Python for application development, automation, data processing, and backend services.\nExperience building and supporting Python-based APIs or web services, preferably with FastAPI, Flask, or similar frameworks.\nUnderstanding of core Python concepts such as object-oriented programming, modular code structure, exception handling, and reusable component design.\nExperience working with API request/response patterns, JSON payloads, validation, authentication, and integration error handling.\nAbility to write asynchronous or concurrent Python code when needed for service integrations or long-running processes.\nExperience debugging Python applications, reviewing logs, identifying root causes, and resolving production issues.\nExperience writing secure and efficient database-driven code using Python and SQL.\nFamiliarity with testing and quality practices such as unit testing, integration testing, and code review.\nAbility to maintain readable, well-documented code and contribute to ongoing modernization and process improvement efforts.\nTechnical Environment\nProgramming / Scripting: Python, SQL\nBackend / API: REST APIs, FastAPI or similar Python web frameworks, service integrations, JSON-based interfaces\nDatabases: Oracle, MySQL, MariaDB, DB2, PL/SQL, relational database concepts\nTools / DevOps: Azure DevOps, Git, GitHub, CI/CD pipelines, Docker, Kubernetes/AKS\nCollaboration: Microsoft Teams, remote collaboration tools, stakeholder communication\nOperating Model: Agile delivery, backlog/story management, production support, after-hours support as needed\nEven Better\nExperience in telecommunications, network automation, service provisioning, or operational support environments.\nExperience with cloud platforms, containerized deployments, and CI/CD delivery practices.\nExperience supporting integrations with vendor or third-party systems.\nFrontend experience with JavaScript, TypeScript, React, or Next.js is a plus, but not required.\nPhysical Tasks- Standing Occasionally: 0-33% | Walking Occasionally: 0-33% |Sitting Continuously: 67-100% | Bending: Occasionally: 0-33% | Crouching: Occasionally: 0-33% | Pushing-Pulling: Occasionally: 0-33% | Carrying: Occasional: 0-33% | Reaching Above Head: Occasionally: 0-33% | Lifting-Lowering >1-15 lbs: Occasionally: 0-33% | Repetitive Hand Action: Medium Dexterity: Continuously: 67-100% | Fine Manipulating: frequently: 34% - 66%\nAudio Visual Needs - Hearing: Continuously: 67-100%| Near Vision: Continuously: 67-100% | Far Vision: Occasionally: 0-33% | Peripheral Vision: Occasionally: 0-33%\nEquipment Used in Job Performance: Computer, Printer, Telephone, Basic Office Supplies, Copier\nThe starting compensation range for this job is $67,100 to $88,000. Our compensation approach is designed to be fair and competitive. Pay for this role is based on factors such as your experience, skills, education, and location.\n_________________________________________________________\nActual base pay for this job will depend on the candidate's primary work location and other factors, such as relevant skills and experience.\nOur Benefits\nMedical, Dental, Vision Insurance Plans\n401K Plan\nHealth & Flexible Savings Account\nLife and AD&D, Spousal Life, Child Life Insurance Plans\nEducational Assistance Plan\nUniti is an equal opportunity employer. At Uniti, we celebrate the authenticity and uniqueness of our people and their ideas. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, genetic information, protected veteran status, current military status, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, creed, citizenship status, or any other status protected by law, and to give full consideration to qualified disabled individuals and protected veterans.\nNotice to Non-U.S. Citizens: Uniti, as a holder of licenses granted by the Federal Communications Commission, is required to notify and to obtain approval from federal regulatory agencies prior to granting certain system/network access to any non-U.S. citizen personnel. Offers of employment extended to non-U.S. citizens are contingent upon receiving the requisite approval from agencies overseeing compliance. Non-U.S. citizens are required to provide Uniti with the personal identifying information required to obtain the necessary approval prior to accessing certain systems and/or Uniti’s network. If you are not a U.S. citizen, please notify your recruiter or contact HR Legal as soon as possible for information on Uniti’s foreign personnel disclosure and approval requirements.\nNotice to Applicants: Depending on the position and its job functions, offers of employment may be contingent upon successful completion of certain pre-employment screenings, including but not limited to drug-screen, motor vehicle records check, or other pre-employment screening. All such screenings will be conducted by an external third-party with the Candidate’s written consent and in accordance with federal and state law. Refusal to authorize or submit to a required pre-employment screening may disqualify the candidate from employment. Any misrepresentation during the application or interview process may result in denial of employment, withdrawal of offer, or termination.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4485263479": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-31T05:53:06.350550+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About the job\nMeeBoss is sharing this active opportunity on behalf of Voltus, a leading company for Distributed Energy Resources (DERs) that aims to be the platform fulfilling the promise of the energy transition.\nThis role is appropriate for entry-level to early-career engineering candidates eager to build scalable software for Voltus.\nYou will join a fully remote team tackling complex energy industry challenges, collaborating with experienced engineers on a modern tech stack, and contributing to core systems that decarbonize the grid.\nJob title\nSoftware Engineer\nCompany\nMeeBoss\nLocation\nRemote\nCompensation\nBase pay is $110,000-$140,000 USD annually, commensurate with experience, with a 10% annual bonus and equity.\nWhy this role\nJoin a fully remote team distributed across the US, Canada, and abroad.\nContribute to core systems that decarbonize the grid and provide flexibility, reliability, and resilience to the energy market.\nCollaborate with experienced engineers on a modern tech stack including Python, Postgres, Go, FastAPI, and React.\nWhat you will do\nWrite clean, maintainable, and well-tested code to support the team’s projects.\nContribute to the design and implementation of new features and services.\nCollaborate with your team to troubleshoot and resolve issues in the production environment.\nParticipate in code reviews to learn from and contribute to the team’s shared knowledge.\nWork with stakeholders to understand requirements and translate them into technical solutions.\nWhat we are looking for\nA Bachelor’s degree, or equivalent combination of education and experience, in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related technical field.\nFoundational programming skills in a backend language like Python.\nA strong desire to learn and grow as a software engineer.\nExcellent communication and collaboration skills.\nA genuine passion for creating a cleaner, more resilient energy future.\nAuthorization to work in the US or Canada without sponsorship.\nA link to your GitHub account in the application (applications without a GitHub account will not be considered).\nBenefits\nUnlimited PTO for full-time employees.\nParental leave.\nComprehensive benefits package to promote health, wellness, and financial security.\nAbout MeeBoss\nMeeBoss helps job seekers and hiring teams make direct, relevant career connections.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      }
    },
    "updated_at": "2026-10-31T05:53:06.350550+00:00"
  },
